<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Ciam scheme audience forms + default-scheme CIAM-token guard (FR-22, FR-23)</title>
    <phase>1 BFF auth and entitlement</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth code in the BFF JwtBearer configuration (tags auth, bff-api)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive token validation change on every route</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>auth, bff-api, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the Ciam JwtBearer scheme accept the per-customer audience in both forms ({bffAppId} and api://{bffAppId}), and make the default (workforce) scheme reject any CIAM token.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ASP.NET Core authentication expert. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>AuthorizationModule.cs validates Ciam audiences in both forms and the default scheme fails any token whose iss contains ciamlogin.com or whose tid equals Ciam:TenantId; unit tests prove each case.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner 2026-10-10: R3 owns FR-22 and FR-23 (relayed by provisioning; supersedes the 2026-10-09 assumption). Today the Ciam scheme (AuthorizationModule.cs ~60-72) sets a single Audience = Ciam:Audience, and the default scheme has no issuer guard against CIAM tokens. CallerPrincipalResolver.DeterminePlane (:386-395) classifies CIAM by iss ∋ ciamlogin.com or tid == Ciam:TenantId; the guard mirrors that rule. The default scheme also merges AgentToken:CopilotAudience (~100-139) — Copilot tokens must still pass.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.template.json</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModuleCiamTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every route this task adds or modifies is mapped inside the /api/v1/external group (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:60-63) so it inherits the ExternalCollaboration policy and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. No route in this task is mapped outside that group.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No OBO on the external plane: every Dataverse and SPE call this task adds is app-only and scoped to the caller's accessible set (spec NFR-01).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build: more than +5 MB needs written justification; the total must stay at or under 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build only on the net10 SDK (10.0.1xx). Run /conflict-check before opening the PR: Api/ExternalAccess/** and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** are shared with unified-access-control-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A1">The Ciam scheme stays pinned to the /api/v1/external group; this task changes only which audiences it accepts.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The guard is implemented in the default scheme's validation (e.g. JwtBearerEvents.OnTokenValidated failing the context, or an IssuerValidator) and reads Ciam:TenantId from configuration; it never relies on library issuer defaults.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">When Ciam:Audience is empty the Ciam scheme keeps today's behaviour (no audience accepted) — do not widen it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>JwtBearer audience and issuer validation</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read AuthorizationModule.cs fully (default scheme, Ciam scheme, CopilotAudience merge) and CallerPrincipalResolver.DeterminePlane.</step>
    <step order="2">Ciam scheme: build ValidAudiences = { Ciam:Audience, and its other form } (strip or add the api:// prefix); keep ValidateAudience = true.</step>
    <step order="3">Default scheme: add the CIAM guard so a token with iss containing ciamlogin.com, or tid equal to Ciam:TenantId (when configured), fails authentication (401).</step>
    <step order="4">Write unit tests that build the configured JwtBearerOptions and run validation against crafted tokens (signed with a test key) for: Ciam GUID audience, Ciam api:// audience, other customer's app audience, workforce token on default scheme, Copilot-audience token on default scheme, CIAM-issuer token on default scheme, CIAM-tid token on default scheme.</step>
    <step order="5">Seeding proof (security guard): remove the guard, confirm the CIAM-on-default test fails, restore.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-010-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If adding the guard would require changing how any existing internal route authenticates (other than rejecting CIAM tokens), STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>When provisioning's T240d S1 (iv) token shape arrives (notes/coordination/), use it for the FR-22 test tokens; if it contradicts the two forms in the spec, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModuleCiamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Ciam:Audience = {appId}, a CIAM token with aud = {appId} passes the Ciam scheme, and a CIAM token with aud = api://{appId} also passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Ciam:Audience = {appId}, a CIAM token with aud = another customer's app id (either form) fails with 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A token with iss containing ciamlogin.com presented to a default-scheme route fails with 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A token with tid = Ciam:TenantId presented to a default-scheme route fails with 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A normal workforce token and a Copilot-audience token still pass the default scheme.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With Ciam:TenantId unset, the default scheme still rejects iss ∋ ciamlogin.com and otherwise behaves as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seeding proof is recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-22, FR-23; design §4.6 C8 'With T240d'. H13 hard-gate probe (provisioning) exercises the same 401.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting this task, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow the task-execute skill for the mandatory pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
